cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPINO: Software for exoPlanet vIsibility and Nightly Observations"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amadori
    given-names: Francesco
    email: francesco.amadori.97.astro@gmail.com
    affiliation: "INAF Osservatorio Astrofisico di Torino"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1316-1033"
repository-code: "https://github.com/francescoa97outlook/SPINO"
url: "https://spino-exoplanets.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  SPINO is a self-contained Tkinter desktop application for planning exoplanet
  transit and secondary-eclipse phase-coverage observations. It wraps a
  scientific scheduling pipeline (catalog loading, desert filtering, per-planet
  visibility computation, TSM/ESM ranking, telluric-overlap plots) behind an
  editable graphical interface, so that every scheduling parameter is a form
  field rather than a line in a configuration file.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - observation planning
  - transit visibility
  - secondary eclipse
  - astronomy
  - Python
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-07-29"
